tms6747  refused by name: the C6000's LDW faults on a misaligned word and the backend emits no LDNW, so a class under `#pragma pack` is not laid out for this target. cl6x has the same answer from the other side - the C6000 compiler has no `#pragma pack`; its packed structs are `__attribute__((packed))`, which this compiler does not read. The emulator showed the fault first: a 4-byte access at an odd address in main, cycle 3287.
